The reported DNS failure for jeremysitlab.com is not reproducible in the lab.
Every component of the DNS path is healthy. SRV1 (10.5.0.4) is up and fully
reachable — zero packet loss from pc2 (Office A, 10.1.0.101), pc3 (Office B,
10.3.0.100), pc1, and laptop1. The BIND9 daemon (named, PID 30) is running and
actively listening on 10.5.0.4:53 for both UDP and TCP. The authoritative zone
file for jeremysitlab.com is correctly loaded, containing A records for the
apex, srv1.jeremysitlab.com, and a wildcard that covers all other campus
hostnames. All four client hosts have nameserver 10.5.0.4 in /etc/resolv.conf
and nsswitch.conf routes hostname lookups through DNS. End-to-end resolution
was verified by running both dig (using the system resolver, no explicit @server
argument) and nslookup from pc1, pc2, pc3, and laptop1 — every query returned
NOERROR with the correct answer (10.5.0.4) in well under 5 ms.

